This function is used by Krake's resource-based routing system to ensure that only valid resource names are used in the URL path. It is used in conjunction with the <code>@resource</code> decorator, which adds routing information to a function that is wrapped by the decorator. By defining the regular expression used to validate the resource name, the <code>@resource</code> decorator can ensure that only valid resource names are passed to the wrapped function as its first argument.

